{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["And he came up to Hebron — the aggadah appears to be the plain sense: that the verse speaks of Caleb, as it is written: ולו אתן את הארץ אשר דרך בה, and הביאותיו אל הארץ אשר בא שמה וזרעו יורישנה. Therefore 'and he came up to Hebron' — it is Caleb, and he prostrated himself on the burial place of the fathers and prayed that he be delivered from the counsel of the spies. And we find in Joshua that Hebron was given to Caleb, as it is written: ואת שדה העיר ואת חצריה נתנו לכלב בן יפנה באחוזתו. But in any case according to the principal plain sense: each and every one came up to Hebron, for after all they said: וגם בני הענקים ראינו שם בחברון. And it is written: ושם ראינו את הנפילים בני ענק." "Before Zoan of Egypt — according to its plain sense: it was built before Zoan, and besides, an old city is more distinguished than a new city. Since Israel recognized the importance of Zoan, he needed to state that the cities of Israel are more distinguished, and also because of its antiquity there were giants there, who are from the early generations."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:11.176627466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}